{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]Strumming my pain with his [Am]fingers.  [D7]singing my life with his [G]words.
[Em]Killing me softly with [Am]his song.  Killing me softly [D]with [C]his song.
Telling my [G]whole life with [C]his words.
Killing me [Fmaj7]softly,  with his [E]song.
[Am7]I heard he [D]sang the good song.
[G]I heard he [C]had a style.
[Am7]And so I [D]came to see him,
and [Em]listen for a while.
[Am7]And there he [D7]was this young boy
[G]a stranger [B7]to my eyes.
{end_of_verse}

